## 1. The last leftover native `confirm()`

**File:** `components/bot/backtests-tab.tsx`, the delete-run handler (around line 52).

Phase 4 replaced native `confirm()` with the styled `ConfirmDialog` component in two places (`app/app/bots/page.tsx`, `components/bot/settings-tab.tsx`) but missed this third call site: deleting a backtest run from a bot's Backtests tab still pops the browser's unstyled `confirm("Are you sure you want to delete the backtest run from ${dateStr}?")`.

Fix using the exact same pattern as the other two sites: hold `{ id, dateStr } | null` in local state, render one `ConfirmDialog` at the bottom of the tab, title `` `Delete backtest run from ${dateStr}?` ``, description `"This permanently removes the run and its results. This can't be undone."`, `destructive` (default true). Wire the row's delete button to open the dialog instead of calling `confirm()` directly; move the actual delete call into `onConfirm`.

