## 3. Pricing drift risk in `components/billing/plan-comparison.tsx`

The table header hardcodes plan prices as literal strings:

```tsx
<TH className="text-center w-36">Starter (₹799)</TH>
<TH className="text-center w-36">Pro (₹1,999)</TH>
```

These happen to match `PLANS` in `mock/data.ts` today, but they're not derived from it — this is the exact "three surfaces, hand-typed numbers, silently drift apart" bug Phase 4 §3 fixed everywhere else. Fix it the same way: look up `PLANS.find(p => p.id === 'starter')` / `'pro'` and interpolate `formatINR(plan.monthly)` into the header instead of a literal string, so a future price change in `mock/data.ts` propagates here automatically like it now does everywhere else.

