## 4. Remove the typecheck safety-off switch

**File:** `next.config.mjs`

```js
typescript: {
  ignoreBuildErrors: true,
},
```

This flag means a real type error would ship silently instead of failing the build. Now that §2 above gets the codebase to a genuinely clean `tsc --noEmit`, remove this flag entirely so `next build` actually enforces types going forward — that's the whole point of using TypeScript. If removing it causes the build to fail, that means there's a real type error hiding behind this flag right now; fix it, don't re-add the flag.

