## 6. Builder: add the missing small-screen fallback

The original build spec required this and it was never built in any phase: *"The Builder canvas is desktop-primary — on small screens show a clean 'Best experienced on a larger screen' state rather than a broken cramped canvas."*

**File:** `app/app/builder/[botId]/page.tsx` (and `app/app/builder/page.tsx`, the bot-picker/new-bot entry, if it has the same problem — check).

Add a simple viewport check — a `useEffect` + `useState` reading `window.innerWidth < 1024` (Tailwind's `lg` breakpoint, matching the rest of the app's convention) is sufficient, no new dependency needed. Below that width, instead of rendering the full canvas/library/inspector layout, render a centered message: an icon (`Monitor` or `LayoutGrid` from `lucide-react`), "Best experienced on a larger screen", one line explaining the Builder needs room for the canvas and side panels, and a `PillLink` back to `/app/bots`. Match the visual pattern of your existing `EmptyState` component rather than hand-rolling new markup. Resize-responsive is not required — checking on mount is enough; don't over-engineer this with a resize listener unless it's trivial to add.

