## 8. Make the Creator Dashboard actually reachable

**This is a real gap, not polish.** Today the *only* way to ever land on `/app/creator/dashboard` is the one-time redirect at the end of the publish wizard (`app/app/marketplace/publish/[botId]/page.tsx` → `router.push('/app/creator/dashboard')`). It's not in the sidebar, not on the Dashboard, not on `/app/presets`, not on a bot's Overview tab — a user who publishes a preset, then navigates away, has no path back to see their earnings short of typing the URL from memory or using Cmd+K (it is in `lib/search-index.ts`, but that's not discovery, that's only useful if you already know the page exists).

Fix in two places:

### 8.1 Sidebar
**File:** `components/app/app-sidebar.tsx`

Add a conditional nav entry. Import `useWorkspace` and read `s.publishedPresets`. Add to `FOOTER_NAV` (it belongs with Billing conceptually — it's a monetization/earnings page):

```tsx
const publishedPresets = useWorkspace((s) => s.publishedPresets)
// ...
{publishedPresets.length > 0 && (
  <SidebarLink href="/app/creator/dashboard" label="Creator" icon={Wallet} />
)}
```

(Use whichever exact rendering pattern the existing `FOOTER_NAV.map(...)` loop uses — don't hand-roll a separate render path for one conditional item; either add it as a genuine fifth entry in the `FOOTER_NAV` array with a `visible` predicate the map checks, or render it as one extra explicit element right after the mapped list — pick whichever is the smaller diff against the existing component.) Use the `Wallet` icon from `lucide-react` (not yet imported in this file) to visually distinguish it from `CreditCard` (Billing). This does not need to be added to `MOBILE_NAV` — five items on mobile is already full and this is a secondary, infrequent-use page; reachable via the full sidebar on larger screens and via search on mobile.

**Note on why this will show up immediately in your local testing:** `publishedPresets` is seeded from the `PUBLISHED_PRESETS` mock fixture by default (not empty), so this condition will read `true` out of the box for the demo account — that's expected and correct, it mirrors how the rest of the app is pre-seeded with mock bots/runs. A genuinely fresh account (if you ever clear `localStorage`) would correctly hide this until they publish something.

### 8.2 Presets page cross-link
**File:** `app/app/presets/page.tsx`

Near wherever this page already explains the publish flow (its empty-state copy or header area — check what's there today), add a small secondary link when `publishedPresets.length > 0`: a `PillLink` or text link "View creator earnings →" to `/app/creator/dashboard`, so someone who arrives at Presets looking for "where did my published thing go" has a direct path, not just the sidebar.

Do not add an unconditional empty-state to the Creator Dashboard page itself in this phase — it currently has no zero-state handling for `publishedPresets.length === 0` (it just renders an empty table), but since the mock data always seeds at least one entry, this is unlikely to actually surface in practice right now. Note it as a "found but not fixed" item in your summary rather than fixing it — it's a real gap but outside this phase's scope, and building a good empty state for a page nobody with zero presets can currently reach organically (since the nav entry itself is conditional on having presets) is low value right now.

